Fixed #18454 -- Added ability to pass a list of signals to `receiver`.

Added ability to use receiver decorator in the following way:

    @receiver([post_save, post_delete], sender=MyModel)
    def signals_receiver(sender, **kwargs):
        ...

Fixed #18972 -- Refactored bundled wsgi server's chunking algorithm.

Thanks to amosonn at yahoo.com for the report, @doda for the initial patch and
@datagrok for the revamped logic and test case.

Fixed #17431 -- Added send_mail() method to PasswordResetForm.

Credits for the initial patch go to ejucovy;
big thanks to Tim Graham for the review.

Fixed #7599 -- Added get_user_permissions to ModelBackend.

Thanks to @gdub for the report and intial patch and
@charettes and @timgraham for the review.

Fixed #26492 -- Fixed "maximum recursion depth exceeded" migrate error.

A regression introduced in 0d3c616fbb2f49fa7ff6809e5a6777275352b35b;
refs #26351.

Refs #27175 -- Removed an obsolete test comment and DEBUG=True.

As of e62165b898785e890661953c3b2c9c36d98aee57, {% include %}
doesn't silence exceptions.

Refs #34233 -- Used @functools.cache.

Python 3.9+ supports @functools.cache as an alias for
@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None).

Refs #36770 -- Guarded against an endless wait in LiveServerThread.terminate().

terminate() shouldn't assume the main server was started. (A deadlock
from mishandling of in-memory SQLite databases may have occurred.)
